                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Possibly one of the worst platformers I've ever played.\nGraphically, you're yeah, the cube in the title. Exactly a cube. \nThe levels are a big background made up by one colour only and the levels are all like this, two rows that you've got to pass since the exit door will always be up above of you.\nThe music is terribly annoying and the worst thing is that it's a MIDI loop that every time you die starts from the beginning. And you will die a lot. Even on the first level. The first obstacle of the first level.\nThe hitbox is huge and you'll die thousands of times only while trying to jump between static obstacles.. and then you'll also have monsters and moving obstacles.\nIn the settings you can choose from windowed or full screen mode, but nothing else. The controls are only WASD and escape, nothing else.\nLuckily it's so fast and easy to load that every time you die (as I said, thousands of times per level) you'll instantly respawn (with the music abruptly stopping and re-starting from the beginning), but anyways it becomes frustrating from the first level and there's 24 of them.\nI recognize that it's the effort of a single Russian developer (if you go windowed, you'll have a bar on the upper side written only in Russian) but really, 2€ for a game like this is one of the worst things the Steam store could possibly offer in my opinion.\nGoing back a little bit to the game, as I said it's an extremely basic platformer. Your goal will be to get to the door and when I was talking about the obstacles maybe I have been too quick. It's not that there are few of them, the big problem is that everything is extremely hard to overcome and it seems that really no one has ever tested a single level (by the way, every level will be open from the menu so that you can complete some later levels that are in fact easier than the first ones). You'll have to deal with crosses going up and down at an extreme velocity, or monsters (which are blocks like you, colored in a different way) that run twice fast as you.\nIt's really frustrating, everything. I'm not saying that it's impossible to play, but really as a platformer I've never seen probably something so badly realized and developed.\nAnd it's also filled with bugs; apart from the hitbox that will make you die by almost being in the zone of everything, some of the static white bars/obstacles allow you to place yourself over them so that you clearly see your character being half over the obstacle, while many of them instantly kill you only by a touch.\nI'm not against hard games, although I like the games which 1. allow you to choose a difficulty setting or 2. have an increasing difficulty curve that goes on with your knowledge and accompanies you from the easiest through the hardest levels. But this is beyond hard, it's stupidly hard since it's not meant to be hard, it's so difficult due to the poorly developed system and the insane amount of moving and static obstacles put in every single level.\nSo, even if you're looking for a hard platformer, I warmly suggest you to avoid this game completely.\nI'd like to suggest you some levels (7, 9 or 10 maybe) if you wanna try the \"easiest\" ones but really, it's utterly frustrating and would not deserve a playthrough even if it was for free, let alone for 2€.",
